WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
What if a scientific claim could end in one of three honest states?

00:05.000 --> 00:12.000
For the Lorenz system, a finite simulation draws the familiar attractor. It is evidence, not proof.

00:12.000 --> 00:20.000
Proved: V stays at most 1600 for every time t at or after zero.

00:20.000 --> 00:27.000
Refuted: V stays at most 1300. The initial state already has V equal to 1371.

00:27.000 --> 00:34.000
Unresolved: V stays at most 1400. This bounded search found neither proof nor checked counterexample.

00:34.000 --> 00:40.000
The same proof, refutation, and unresolved outcome appears on a second three-mode system. Inspect every receipt in the notebooks.
